<title>USA: PECO sees two 380 MW Pa. units back today.</title>
<headline>PECO sees two 380 MW Pa. units back today.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>PECO Energy Co said Monday two 380 megawatt (MW) units at its Eddystone, Pa., generation station would likely come back on line some time today.</p>
<p>The units, which consume fuel oil and/or natural gas, were taken out of service this past weekend due to weak power demand linked to the region's unseasonally mild autumn weather, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>Two neighboring coal-fired units, each at 270 MW, were running at full ouput, he added.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
</text>
